a. caring for, maintaining, educating, and protecting children;
b. developing children according to their abilities, talents and interests;
c. preventing the occurrence of marriage at child age;
d. preventing the occurrence of acts of violence against women and children;
e. providing information and/or reporting acts of violence against women and children victims of violence to law enforcers or authorized parties; and
f. participating in the handling of victims of acts of violence.
3. In the event that parents do not exist, or their whereabouts are unknown, or due to a certain reason, cannot carry out their obligations and responsibilities, then the obligations and responsibilities as referred to in paragraph (1), may be transferred to the family, which shall be implemented in accordance with the provisions of Laws and Regulations.
